      "updated": 1791994556629,
      "created": 1791994033116,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\n2. this is determined ->\n\n        by who called the fxn\n\n            user1.greet()\n            user2.greet() \n\n        even user2 have a greet prop that call inside \n            user1.greet()\n        still -> the greet() gonna get resolved the this\n            from the right side of . means from user2\n\n      ii) arrowfunction ->\n                do not get there own this \n                use the lexical scope this -> lexical means\n                            the scope of block { }\n                                in which => fxn exists\n      \n      iii) .call on the function-> \n                u can write .call(pass_obj) on function\n                and now fxn will get its this from pass_obj  ",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\n2. this is determined ->\n\n        by who called the fxn\n\n            user1.greet()\n            user2.greet() \n\n        even user2 have a greet prop that call inside \n            user1.greet()\n        still -> the greet() gonna get resolved the this\n            from the right side of . means from user2\n\n      ii) arrowfunction ->\n                do not get there own this \n                use the lexical scope this -> lexical means\n                            the scope of block { }\n                                in which => fxn exists\n      \n      iii) .call on the function-> \n                u can write .call(pass_obj) on function\n                and now fxn will get its this from pass_obj       ",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
