      "updated": 1792010408253,
      "created": 1791981188072,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1.  why i can't write function keyword in a class -> to define a fxn \n\nMechanism: the parser has \"modes\"\n\nBefore running anything, the compiler reads your text and checks it\nagainst grammar rules. Those rules depend on where you are:\n\nTop level of the file: it accepts function, class, const, let.\nInside class { ... }: it only accepts fields, a constructor, and methods\nwritten as name() {}.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1.  why i can't write function keyword in a class -> to define a fxn \n\nMechanism: the parser has \"modes\"\n\nBefore running anything, the compiler reads your text and checks it against grammar rules. Those rules depend on where you are:\n\nTop level of the file: it accepts function, class, const, let.\nInside class { ... }: it only accepts fields, a constructor, and methods written as name() {}.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
